      "message": "test(3d): re-pin the pocket3d_hsm bore after the solidcore bump\n\nThe heavy step `app heavy: pocket3d_hsm` was red on main since the merge\nof PR #3802 (df899f029, the solidcore bump). The bump meshes\nMilling-test.step to 5232 facets (6228 before). The HSM planner code did\nnot change. Each level still takes one of the two plans that the bore had\nbefore; the new mesh moves which levels take the long plan (Z 10 before,\nZ 15 and Z 5 now). Every level verifies clean and none falls back.\n\nLinux x86_64, release: 940cc5d0e gives 6228 facets and\n(3158, 3130, 1141); df899f029 and baad348f1 give 5232 facets and\n(4688, 4660, 1980). Windows gave the same new triple at 6d0381f19 and\n2e2d40cb3. macOS arm64 is not measured after the bump.\n\nThe long plan (999.92 mm against 334.31 mm of feed) is an older planner\ndefect, filed as #4010.\n\nFixes #3886\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
